	"modules": {
		"@okikio/streams": {
			"module_doc": {
				"doc": "Consume asynchronous data with explicit item, byte and line budgets. A successful Array.fromAsync can still exhaust memory if the source never ends or one record is enormous.\n\nBatch for database writes, fold streams without collecting, and use bounded collect() only when a finite materialized result is needed. Pass cancellation into the source operation as well as the adapter. Early iteration exit cancels owned Web streams unless preventCancel explicitly keeps borrowed ownership. Byte estimates for object batches are caller policy; line framing counts actual encoded bytes.\n",
				"tags": [
					{
						"kind": "example",
						"doc": "```ts\nimport * as streams from '@okikio/streams';\nconst batches = streams.batch(['a', 'b', 'c'], { maximumItems: 2 });\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(await Array.fromAsync(batches)));\nconst bytes = new Response(`first\nsecond\n`).body!;\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(await Array.fromAsync(streams.lines(bytes, { maximumLineBytes: 64 }))));\n```\n"
					},
					{
						"kind": "module"
					}
				]
			},
